{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"capillary-seared-grackle","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/integration cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py:1-21` — Preserve real Git-bundle model, injected S3 surface, and lossless-heal oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py:1-12, 279-282` — Preserve snapshot-only state, retired-source recovery, and per-UUID history fallback. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py:1-71` — Preserve `safe.bareRepository=explicit` behavior, accepted `--git-dir` form, scanner scope, and exclusions. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:1-19, 79-90, 102-112, 121-142, 148-164, 324-330, 422-426, 442-456, 804-813, 1054-1061, 1325-1328, 1374-1380, 1420-1425, 1492-1501, 1506-1517, 1619-1634, 1665-1676, 1721-1724, 1755-1767, 1851-1855, 1876-1880, 1904-1924, 2190-2198` — Preserve deterministic barriers, union/convergence invariants, exact fork winners, repair ordering, parent-cascade races, and append-only history. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py:1-17` — Preserve seed/stamp effects and no-per-ticket-event migration invariant. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_id_collision.py:1-19` — Preserve canonical-ID shape, deterministic aliases, and meaningful collision checks. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py:639-656` — Preserve requirement that template-copy source remotes have no active detached upkeep. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:1-42, 59-67, 84-92, 328-334, 394-412, 462-476, 523-529, 571-577, 595-606` — Preserve bilateral cleanup, xdist confinement, import isolation, fresh-client polling, eventual-consistency budget, and memoization regression oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:1-21` — Preserve the held-out edge-case inventory and non-implementation exposure. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py:1-15, 131-139, 203-209` — Preserve lossless heal, bounded transient retry, and published-ref targeting. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py:1-14` — Preserve fail-closed requirement and required helper capability. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py:1-19, 131-135` — Preserve concurrent-writer zero-loss/fsck oracle. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py tests/integration/test_id_collision.py tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"46e0-1134-708b-4752","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/integration"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571030445200204,"uuid":"88bf9a60-7636-4ef5-b45d-2be1026aec87"}